several PKC isoforms including alpha, beta, delta and zeta isoforms. Their activation is preceded by the activation of PLC gamma (Suzuma et al. 2002, Xia et al. 1996, Takahashi et al. 1999, Wellner et al. 1999). Before Protein kinase C (PKC) is competent to respond to second messengers it must first be phosphorylated at three conserved positions: the activation loop and two positions at the carboxyl terminus of the protein (Dutil et al. 1998). The phosphorylation of the activation loop appears to occur first and is mediated by phosphoinositide dependent protein kinases (PDKs). PDK1 phosphorylates PKCs at a critical Thr (T) residue in the activation loop, a requirement for PKC to gain catalytic competency (Toker 2003).", "literatureReference": [5218368, 4332315, {"dbId": 5218512, "displayName": "Characterization of vascular endothelial growth factor's effect on the activation of protein kinase C, its isoforms, and endothelial cell growth", "title": "Characterization of vascular endothelial growth factor's effect on the activation of protein kinase C, its isoforms, and endothelial cell growth", "journal": "J. Clin. Invest.", "pages": "2018-26", "pubMedIdentifier": 8903320, "volume": 98, "year": 1996, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/8903320", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 5218448, "displayName": "The proliferative effect of vascular endothelial growth factor requires protein kinase C-alpha and protein kinase C-zeta", "title": "The proliferative effect of vascular endothelial growth factor requires protein kinase C-alpha and protein kinase C-zeta", "journal": "Arterioscler. Thromb. Vasc. Biol.", "pages": "178-85", "pubMedIdentifier": 9888881, "volume": 19, "year": 1999, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9888881", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 5218378, "displayName": "Characterization of protein kinase C beta isoform's action on retinoblastoma protein phosphorylation, vascular endothelial growth factor-induced endothelial cell proliferation, and retinal neovascularization", "title": "Characterization of protein kinase C beta isoform's action on retinoblastoma protein phosphorylation, vascular endothelial growth factor-induced endothelial cell proliferation, and retinal neovascularization", "journal": "Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. U.S.A.", "pages": "721-6", "pubMedIdentifier": 11805327, "volume": 99, "year": 2002, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11805327", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 5218539, "displayName": "VEGF activates protein kinase C-dependent, but Ras-independent Raf-MEK-MAP kinase pathway for DNA synthesis in primary endothelial cells", "title": "VEGF activates protein kinase C-dependent, but Ras-independent Raf-MEK-MAP kinase pathway for DNA synthesis in primary endothelial cells", "journal": "Oncogene", "pages": "2221-30", "pubMedIdentifier": 10327068, "volume": 18, "year": 1999, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/10327068", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}], "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "isChimeric": false, "category": "transition", "catalystActivity": [{"dbId": 377328, "displayName": "protein serine/threonine kinase activity of PDPK1 [plasma membrane]", "catalyzedEvent": [5218821], "physicalEntity": {"dbId": 61459, "displayName": "PDPK1 [plasma membrane]", "stId": "R-HSA-61459", "stIdVersion": "R-HSA-61459.1", "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["PDPK1", "PDK1", "3-phosphoinositide dependent protein kinase-1"], "speciesName": "Homo sapiens", "catalystActivities": [377328], "endCoordinate": 556, "referenceType": "ReferenceGeneProduct", "startCoordinate": 1, "className": "Protein", "inDisease"